// Dialog - Bomb1DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1993431211" "<color orange>You see a tangle of red, green, and black wires leading into the face of what looks to be an old calculator. This crude interface is duct taped to the side of a car battery.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1754756608" "(Examine the detonator)"
// Answer Text :
"P71763962" "(Magic Origin: Cast 'Speak with Lightning Elementals' Spell)"
// Answer Text :
"P2728114494" "(Tech Origin: Cut the hidden blue wire)"
// Page ExaminePage1 Text :
"P3033845547" "<color orange>On top of the calculator is the thermometer from an old air conditioner. If you bump this detonator too much the mercury in the thermometer will cause the glass tube to shift and it will complete the circuit to the car battery, detonating the explosives.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P333501598" "(Examine the wiring)"
// Page WirePage1 Text :
"P1268206478" "<color orange>You look at the mass of wires, but all you see are red, green, and black wires.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3118355390" "(Examine the battery)"
// Page BatteryPage1 Text :
"P3852851925" "<color orange>You examine the battery set up, it's a simple set up. One positive and one negative line. Looking at it you don't see any reason why you couldn't just disconnect them both, assuming you are fast enough.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1151638981" "(Disconnect the Battery)"
// Page BatteryPage2 Text :
"P3114569329" "<color orange>With luck, determination, and a little more agility than the average person you wrap your fingers around the positive and negative clamps and with a swift tug, detach them both at the same instant. Only two words can explain how relieved you are when you see the calculator turn off.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1517400020" "Leave"
// Page MagicPage1 Text :
"P1551798393" "<color orange>A tiny excited voice sizzles and pops from the car battery.</color><br><br>"Hi!""
// Answer Text :
"P3199374967" "(Ask the elemental to leave)"
// Page MagicPage2 Text :
"P2744687343" "<color orange>The tiny voice buzzes cutely.</color><br><br>"Yes {Hero.gender=male master|mistress}."<br><br><color orange>With a pop and a wiff of ozone, the elemental is gone and the numbers counting down on the calculator fade away.</color>"
// Page TechPage1 Text :
"P3607335744" "<color>You cut the blue wire, the one hidden under black electrical tape. Oldest trick in the book, right next to installing a red light next to a mass of blue, green, and brown wires.<br><br>The numbers on the calculator stop.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1187024072" "I checked with one of my contacts down in the tunnels. She's a mousey little thing, but she knows the tunnels like the back of her hand.<br><br>She told me that the tunnels have been crawling with Destroyers and Crusader squads all day. They all seem to be convening under People's Park, according to her.<br><br>{HeroName}, it sounds like Pain God and his Destroyers were just one little piece of a massive puzzle, and I don't know about you, but that puzzle is starting to take frightening shape.<br><br>High explosives, a war? I think they're planning on blowing up something big..."
// AcceptString :
"P3900244174" "Like a skyscraper?"
// SendOffString :
"P2706368816" "...!<br><br>Holy... You're right! If they toppled a skyscraper in the middle of downtown... The devastation would be incacu...incalul...incaculb...hard to calculate!<br><br><color orange>Find the meeting place in the tunnels.</color> I'll see if Tunnel Rat can get you some help. We've got to act fast!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2733022943" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: The Aureas TNT Party</color>"

